cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "EIGER: label-free discovery of regionally coordinated DNA methylation"
abstract: >-
  EIGER finds regions of coordinated DNA methylation without predefined sample
  groups: runs of neighbouring CpGs whose methylation co-varies across samples.
  Each candidate region receives a coordination q-value from complete
  within-CpG permutation rescans of the data, and optional descriptive
  annotations of how the region follows genome-wide sample axes. The
  originally published covariance statistic is available with --legacy.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Milne-Clark
    given-names: Toby
version: "2.2.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tobymilnec/EIGER"
keywords:
  - DNA methylation
  - differentially methylated regions
  - whole-genome bisulfite sequencing
  - false discovery rate
  - unsupervised
